1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:04,851
Did a woman U.S. officials suspect of spying for China get close to the most powerful man in AI?

2
00:00:05,171 --> 00:00:11,131
Meet Alice Huang, no relation, former CEO of Megaspeed, a Singapore firm renting out NVIDIA computing power.

3
00:00:11,451 --> 00:00:15,292
Bloomberg estimates it imported at least $4.6 billion of NVIDIA hardware.

4
00:00:15,472 --> 00:00:17,388
Its largest client, reports say: Alibaba.

5
00:00:17,708 --> 00:00:20,774
Renting that power abroad wasn't banned. Shipping chips into China was.

6
00:00:20,954 --> 00:00:24,426
Investigators are probing whether chips crossed that line. No charges have been filed.

7
00:00:24,746 --> 00:00:29,994
The New York Times reported officials suspect she worked with Chinese intelligence, and had a relationship with Jensen Huang.

8
00:00:30,314 --> 00:00:31,951
Reuters says he called it routine business.

9
00:00:32,271 --> 00:00:33,544
On November 12, he resigned.

10
00:00:33,864 --> 00:00:36,805
China calls the claims groundless. Megaspeed denies wrongdoing.

11
00:00:37,125 --> 00:00:41,512
So, did America's top AI tech leak? NVIDIA's board says it has no reason to believe so.

12
00:00:41,832 --> 00:00:42,711
Follow InvisiTech.

